Containers
==========

Seam: a list, a tuple, the unit, the 1-tuple, the 15-tuple limit, a
range, an iterator and an exhausted one, nested and shared data (memo A2).
Catalogue: P8 (the 16-tuple), P9 (iterators).  Issues: none.
Output: a list crosses with one element type, so [1, 2.5] is [1.0, 2.5] of
type Fractional a => [a].  () is the unit; (1,) is a ConversionError.  The
14-tuple comes back as a Python tuple.  The 15-tuple crosses in and types,
but the converter stops at 14 components and hands back the node, which
prints in its raw form.  The 16-tuple types and then fails as a
SymbolLookupError on a symbol the user never wrote (P8).  range(3) has no
row in the table; list(range(3)) crosses.  An iterator is a lazy list:
take 3 of itertools.count(10) is [10, 11, 12], and iter([1, 2]) has length
2 at its first use and 0 at the second (P9).  A Python list used twice in
one tuple crosses as a pair of equal lists.
Oracle: oracle.out holds the PAKCS 3.4.1 transcripts of the plain goals.
Backends: py and cxx, one output.
